From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 11:35:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Honour empty clip regions

An inset() whose opposing insets meet or cross resolves to an empty
clip region, which per css-masking hides the element entirely. The Rect
arm returned None, and the caller reads None as "no clip-path" and
pushes no layer at all, so the element painted at full size: the exact
inverse of what an empty region means. Clamp the far edges to the near
ones so the rect stays empty instead of inverting into a mirrored
region.

inset(50%) is one of the spellings visually-hidden labels use, so it
rendered the label at full size. The other, `clip: rect(0,0,0,0)`, is
handled by upstream's CSS 2 `clip` support.
---
 src/render/clip_path.rs | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/render/clip_path.rs b/src/render/clip_path.rs
index 9f23e03..674b033 100644
--- a/src/render/clip_path.rs
+++ b/src/render/clip_path.rs
@@ -157,12 +157,10 @@ impl ElementCx<'_, '_> {

                 let x0 = ox + left;
                 let y0 = oy + top;
-                let x1 = ox + w - right;
-                let y1 = oy + h - bottom;
-
-                if x1 <= x0 || y1 <= y0 {
-                    return None;
-                }
+                // Insets that meet or cross over leave an empty region, which clips the
+                // element away; clamping keeps the rect empty rather than inverting it.
+                let x1 = (ox + w - right).max(x0);
+                let y1 = (oy + h - bottom).max(y0);

                 // TODO: Support border-radius on inset()
                 Some(kurbo::Rect::new(x0, y0, x1, y1).into_path(0.1))
